IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-interpretation`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 15 to 18 (the offences), 17A (insurance) and 22 (penalties) -- layer 1.
-- Each offence is a test over the elements the section states.  "A person commits an offence if ..." gives
-- JUST TRUE when every element is present.  When one is missing, JUST FALSE answers only "this provision does not
-- make it an offence" (the text's "if"; NOTES.md, Marginal readings, M1): whether some other provision does is the
-- question that provision answers.  A penalty is a ceiling, never an amount to be paid.
-- "For the purposes of terrorism" is a fact the caller states; section 1 of the Act is not among the sources.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Offences`

§§ `s 15 Fund-raising`

-- src:22 | (4) In this section a reference to the provision of money or other property is a reference to its being given, lent or otherwise made available, whether or not for consideration.
@ref s 15(4) (src:22)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Fund-raising act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(4) the person provides money or other property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act`'s `gives it` OR `the act`'s `lends it` OR `the act`'s `otherwise makes it available`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a reference to its being given, lent or otherwise made available, whether or not for consideration"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:13 | (1) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:14 | (a) invites another to provide money or other property, and
-- src:15 | (b) intends that it should be used, or has reasonable cause to suspect that it may be used, for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 15(1) (src:13-15)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Fund-raising act`
      `the person's state of mind` IS A `Mind about use for terrorism`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(1) the person commits an offence by inviting another to provide money or other property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act`'s `invites another to provide it`
           AND (`the person's state of mind`'s `intends that it should be used`
                OR `the person's state of mind`'s `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:16 | (2) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:17 | (a) receives money or other property, and
-- src:18 | (b) intends that it should be used, or has reasonable cause to suspect that it may be used, for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 15(2) (src:16-18)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Fund-raising act`
      `the person's state of mind` IS A `Mind about use for terrorism`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(2) the person commits an offence by receiving money or other property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act`'s `receives it`
           AND (`the person's state of mind`'s `intends that it should be used`
                OR `the person's state of mind`'s `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:19 | (3) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:20 | (a) provides money or other property, and
-- src:21 | (b) knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used for the purposes of terrorism.
-- src:22 | (4) In this section a reference to the provision of money or other property is a reference to its being given, lent or otherwise made available, whether or not for consideration.
@ref s 15(3) (src:19-21) (src:22)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Fund-raising act`
      `the person's state of mind` IS A `Mind about use for terrorism`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(3) the person commits an offence by providing money or other property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 15(4) the person provides money or other property` `the act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (`the person's state of mind`'s `knows that it will be used`
                OR `the person's state of mind`'s `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 Use and possession`

-- src:24 | (1) A person commits an offence if he uses money or other property for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 16(1) (src:24)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Use and possession act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(1) the person commits an offence by using money or other property for the purposes of terrorism` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act`'s `uses it for the purposes of terrorism`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he uses money or other property for the purposes of terrorism."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:25 | (2) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:26 | (a) possesses money or other property, and
-- src:27 | (b) intends that it should be used, or has reasonable cause to suspect that it may be used, for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 16(2) (src:25-27)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Use and possession act`
      `the person's state of mind` IS A `Mind about use for terrorism`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(2) the person commits an offence by possessing money or other property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act`'s `possesses it`
           AND (`the person's state of mind`'s `intends that it should be used`
                OR `the person's state of mind`'s `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 17 Funding arrangements`

-- src:29 | A person commits an offence if—
-- src:30 | (a) he enters into or becomes concerned in an arrangement as a result of which money or other property is made available or is to be made available to another, and
-- src:31 | (b) he knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 17 (src:29-31)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Arrangement act`
      `the person's state of mind` IS A `Mind about use for terrorism`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 the person commits an offence by a funding arrangement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the act`'s `enters into an arrangement` OR `the act`'s `becomes concerned in an arrangement`)
           AND `the act`'s `as a result money or other property is or is to be made available to another`
           AND (`the person's state of mind`'s `knows that it will be used`
                OR `the person's state of mind`'s `reasonable cause to suspect that it will or may be used`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 17A Insurance against payments made in response to terrorist demands`

-- src:33 | (1) The insurer under an insurance contract commits an offence if—
-- src:34 | (a) the insurer makes a payment under the contract, or purportedly under it,
-- src:35 | (b) the payment is made in respect of any money or other property that has been, or is to be, handed over in response to a demand made wholly or partly for the purposes of terrorism, and
-- src:36 | (c) the insurer or the person authorising the payment on the insurer's behalf knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that the money or other property has been, or is to be, handed over in response to such a demand.
@ref s 17A(1) (src:33-36)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Insurance payment facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17A(1) the insurer commits an offence by paying under the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment`'s `the person is the insurer under an insurance contract`
           AND `the payment`'s `payment made under the contract or purportedly under it`
           AND `the payment`'s `payment in respect of money or other property handed over or to be handed over in response to a demand made wholly or partly for the purposes of terrorism`
           AND (`the payment`'s `the insurer knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it was or is to be handed over in response to such a demand`
                OR `the payment`'s `the person authorising the payment on the insurer's behalf knows or has reasonable cause to suspect that it was or is to be handed over in response to such a demand`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The insurer under an insurance contract commits an offence if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:37 | (2) If an offence under this section committed by a body corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of—
-- src:38 | (a) a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate, or
-- src:39 | (b) any person who was purporting to act in any such capacity,
-- src:40 | that person, as well as the body corporate, is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 17A(2) (src:37-40)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Officer liability facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17A(2) the officer is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `offence under s 17A committed by a body corporate`
           AND (`the facts`'s `proved to have been committed with the person's consent or connivance`
                OR `the facts`'s `proved to be attributable to neglect on the person's part`)
           AND (`the facts`'s `the person is a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the body corporate`
                OR `the facts`'s `the person was purporting to act in such a capacity`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offence under this section committed by a body corporate is proved to have been committed"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:41 | (3) The reference in subsection (2) to a director, in relation to a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members, is a reference to a member of the body corporate.
@ref s 17A(3) (src:41)
GIVEN `the body corporate's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17A(3) the person is the body corporate's director for the purposes of s 17A(2)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body corporate's affairs are managed by its members` AND `the person is a member of the body corporate`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a reference to a member of the body corporate" (a person who is not a member is not the reference)
        IF `the body corporate's affairs are managed by its members`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members" (any other body corporate is outside the subsection)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:42 | (4) If an offence under this section is committed by a Scottish partnership and is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of—
-- src:43 | (a) a partner, or
-- src:44 | (b) any person who was purporting to act in that capacity,
-- src:45 | that person, as well as the partnership, is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 17A(4) (src:42-45)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Officer liability facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17A(4) the partner is guilty of the offence as well as the partnership` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `offence under s 17A committed by a Scottish partnership`
           AND (`the facts`'s `proved to have been committed with the person's consent or connivance`
                OR `the facts`'s `proved to be attributable to neglect on the person's part`)
           AND (`the facts`'s `the person is a partner`
                OR `the facts`'s `the person was purporting to act in such a capacity`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offence under this section is committed by a Scottish partnership and is proved to have been committed"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:46 | (5) In this section “insurance contract” means a contract under which one party accepts significant insurance risk from another party (“the policyholder”) by agreeing to compensate the policyholder if a specified uncertain future event adversely affects the policyholder.
@ref s 17A(5) (src:46)
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Contract facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17A(5) the contract is an insurance contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract`'s `one party accepts significant insurance risk from another party`
           AND `the contract`'s `by agreeing to compensate the other party if a specified uncertain future event adversely affects that party`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“insurance contract” means a contract under which"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 18 Money laundering`

-- src:48 | (1) A person commits an offence if he enters into or becomes concerned in an arrangement which facilitates the retention or control by or on behalf of another person of terrorist property—
-- src:49 | (a) by concealment,
-- src:50 | (b) by removal from the jurisdiction,
-- src:51 | (c) by transfer to nominees, or
-- src:52 | (d) in any other way.
@ref s 18(1) (src:48-52)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Laundering act`
      `the facts about the property` IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) the person commits an offence by an arrangement that facilitates retention or control of terrorist property` IS
    IF (`the act`'s `enters into an arrangement` OR `the act`'s `becomes concerned in an arrangement`)
       AND (`the act`'s `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by concealment`
            OR `the act`'s `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by removal from the jurisdiction`
            OR `the act`'s `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person by transfer to nominees`
            OR `the act`'s `the arrangement facilitates retention or control by or on behalf of another person in any other way`)
    -- the last element is "terrorist property": s 14(1) answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE (a closed definition), and the answer is carried as it is
    THEN `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` `the facts about the property`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he enters into or becomes concerned in an arrangement which facilitates"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:53 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (1) to prove that he did not know and had no reasonable cause to suspect that the arrangement related to terrorist property.
@ref s 18(2) (src:53)
GIVEN `charged with an offence under s 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proof` IS A `Proof about terrorist property`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- JUST FALSE here means only: this section gives no defence on these facts.
-- It does not say the person has no defence at all, because another provision (s 19(3), s 21(5), s 21ZC) may still give one.
DECIDE `s 18(2) the person has a defence` IS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person charged with an offence under subsection (1)" (a person not so charged is outside the grant: a scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); assumed, not ruled, that this limb is a scope limit and not part of the proof, fork F18)
        IF (NOT `charged with an offence under s 18(1)`)
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `the proof`'s `proves that he did not know that the arrangement related to terrorist property`
           AND `the proof`'s `proves that he had no reasonable cause to suspect that the arrangement related to terrorist property`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (1) to prove that he did not know and had no reasonable cause to suspect" (the proof is not made, on either limb: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); this section gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 22 Penalties`

-- src:417 | A person guilty of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 shall be liable—
-- src:418 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years, to a fine or to both, or
-- src:419 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both.
@ref s 22 (src:417-419)
GIVEN `the route of conviction` IS A `Conviction route`
      `the statutory maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
DECIDE `s 22 the ceiling of the penalty for an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS
    CONSIDER `the route of conviction`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF (14 TIMES 12), `No ceiling is stated`
                                            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine or to both" states no ceiling for the fine
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF 6, `A fine not exceeding` `the statutory maximum`
